.TH "GYRO" "1" "Nov 2026" "Gyro Hosting" "gyro manual"

.SH NAME
gyro - Gyro Hosting command-line interface


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgyro [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
gyro manages your Gyro Hosting services from the terminal: cloud servers, SSH keys, invoices,
balance and everything else the Gyro Public API offers (API spec 2.17.4).

.PP
Get started:
  gyro configure                 # store an API key (Client area → account menu (top right) → API Credentials)
  gyro server list
  gyro server create --plan standart-2-4 --location falkenstein --image ubuntu-24.04 --ssh-key mykey --wait
  gyro server ssh web-1

.PP
Money and destructive actions ask for confirmation (use --yes in scripts, --dry-run for a quote).


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--api-url\fP=""
	API base URL (env GYRO_API_URL)

.PP
\fB--debug\fP[=false]
	log HTTP requests to stderr (secrets masked)

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for gyro

.PP
\fB--lang\fP=""
	message language: tr or en (default from locale)

.PP
\fB--no-color\fP[=false]
	disable colours (also NO_COLOR)

.PP
\fB--no-header\fP[=false]
	omit the table header

.PP
\fB-o\fP, \fB--output\fP=""
	output format: table, json, yaml, text

.PP
\fB-p\fP, \fB--profile\fP=""
	profile to use (env GYRO_PROFILE)

.PP
\fB--query\fP=""
	JMESPath query applied to the result

.PP
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP[=false]
	print only ids

.PP
\fB--timeout\fP=0s
	overall timeout, e.g. 30s, 10m

.PP
\fB--wide\fP[=false]
	show all table columns

.PP
\fB-y\fP, \fB--yes\fP[=false]
	do not ask for confirmation


